{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cities, and serene gardens. My recent trip lived up to every expectation and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Neon lights blazed, the aroma of ramen filled the air, and the sheer energy of Shibuya Crossing was exhilarating. I spent days exploring quirky neighborhoods like Harajuku and Akihabara, indulging in delicious street food, and marveling at the futuristic architecture.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The contrast was stunning. Kyoto offered a glimpse into traditional Japan – geishas gracefully gliding through Gion, stunning temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion), and peaceful bamboo forests. I wandered through Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates, feeling a sense of calm I hadn't realized I was missing.\n\nThe food was incredible throughout the entire journey. From fresh sushi and delicate tempura to hearty okonomiyaki, every meal was a delight. \n\nNavigating the language barrier was a challenge, but the kindness and helpfulness of the Japanese people shone through. I got wonderfully lost (and found!) countless times, discovering hidden gems and experiencing the true heart of Japan. It’s a country that effortlessly blends tradition and innovation, and I can't wait to go back.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011843579122796655}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.16028544306755066}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0018123644404113293}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.14268149435520172}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.07544055581092834}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.21004177629947662